To install, as ansible on ansible-forge:

cp /opt/ansible/nucleus/playbooks/build_grafana_stack.yml{,.pre-split}
tar -xzf grafana-quarterly-split.tar.gz -C /

Two things outside this task need your attention:

The quarterly trigger doesn’t exist. Ansible’s crontab runs /opt/ansible/scripts/check_new_quarter.sh on the 1st, but Nov 1’s log says No such file or directory. 
Jan 1 won’t start the Q2 build until that’s fixed. If the script lives somewhere else, the crontab path just needs changing.
Old signatures and scan results pile up in each new quarter. The seed copies all of the previous quarter’s provenance files, 
and the clean step never removes old signatures. That’s pre-existing, but IA will see last quarter’s files in every release. It’s an easy follow-up.

As for months or years: your weekly framework did most of the design work here. The new roles copy its layout almost line for line. 
Next up is the same split for Guacamole, which should mostly be a new set of quarterly_component definitions.

